Traccar
-------

Traccar (https://github.com/traccar/traccar)
Copyright Anton Tananaev and Traccar contributors
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

No Traccar source code is included. Traccar was used in three ways:

1. Test data. Device packets published in Traccar's protocol decoder tests
   (src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol) are used, as protocol facts, as
   test vectors in these files:
   - gt06/gt06_test.go: GT06/Concox frames, also quoted in the protocol
     documents.
   - gt06/lbs_test.go: GT06/Concox cell (LBS) and WiFi frames from the GT06
     tests; gt06/lbs.go's frame layouts were checked against them.
   - jt808/decode_test.go: the JT/T 808 frames of the vRegister2013 to
     vRegister2019 block (2013 and 2019 registration, authentication,
     location, locate answer, batch and blind-area uploads, a 0x6006 text
     answer), from Jt808ProtocolDecoderTest.
   - h02/decode_test.go: H02 binary records bDoc, bText and b45.
   - ruptela/ruptela_test.go: Ruptela packets devRecords, devIdent,
     devGetio and devExt.
   - ais140/ais140_test.go: AIS-140 packets of several manufacturers
     (fieldVectors).
   - osmand/decode_test.go: OsmAnd sample requests and older Traccar
     Client JSON bodies (OsmAndProtocolDecoderTest).
   Added in v0.2.0:
   - gt06/more_test.go: GT06 frames (0x10, 0x19, 0x23, 0x27, 0x2A, 0xA0 to
     0xA5, 0x9B, 0x32, 0x33) from Gt06ProtocolDecoderTest.
   - h02: frames quoted in Traccar's H02 tests.
   - teltonika/codec7_test.go: GH codec 7 packets from
     TeltonikaProtocolDecoderTest.
   - queclink/hex_test.go: HEX frames from Gl200BinaryProtocolDecoderTest
     and Gl200FrameDecoderTest.
   - meitrack/vectors_test.go: CCC and D00 packets from
     MeitrackProtocolDecoderTest.
   - ruptela/vectors_test.go: the files packet and trouble-code payload
     from RuptelaProtocolDecoderTest.
   - jt808/ext_test.go: the 0x64 ADAS and a 0x66 frame from
     Jt808ProtocolDecoderTest.
   - ais140/traccar_test.go: every packet of ItsProtocolDecoderTest.
   - wialon/wialon_test.go, galileosky/galileosky_test.go,
     suntech/decode_test.go, calamp/calamp_test.go, atrack, eelink and
     watch tests: device packets from WialonProtocolDecoderTest,
     GalileoProtocolDecoderTest, SuntechProtocolDecoderTest,
     CalAmpProtocolDecoderTest, AtrackProtocolDecoderTest,
     AtrackFrameDecoderTest, EelinkProtocolDecoderTest,
     EelinkProtocolEncoderTest, WatchProtocolDecoderTest,
     WatchFrameDecoderTest and WatchProtocolEncoderTest.

2. Reference reading for facts, without taking code: the H02 decoder
   and encoder, the JT808 decoder and encoder ("huabao"), the OsmAnd
   decoder, and the Position and Device models whose JSON field names a
   Traccar server's position forwarding carries (osmand/json.go reads
   them); for v0.2.0 also the GT06, Teltonika (codec 7), Queclink HEX,
   Meitrack (CCC, D00), Ruptela, ITS, Galileo, Suntech, CalAmp, ATrack,
   Eelink and Watch decoders. PROVENANCE.md says what was taken from each.

3. Interop peer: the traccar/traccar:6.16.0 Docker image is run, unchanged,
   by the tests of trackers-sim's interop module; nothing of it is
   distributed.

go-jt808
--------

cuteLittleDevil/go-jt808 (https://github.com/cuteLittleDevil/go-jt808),
licensed under the MIT License. Its documentation and model files were
read for the JT/T 808 active-safety and JT/T 1078 signalling layouts
(facts); no code was used.

Teltonika AVL ID list
---------------------

IO element IDs, units and multipliers in teltonika/ioelements.go are facts
from Teltonika's public FMB AVL ID list (wiki.teltonika-gps.com); the names
are our own.

Traccar's web site also hosts manufacturers' protocol documents
(traccar.org/protocol/...); those are the manufacturers' documents, cited
in PROVENANCE.md, not Traccar's work.

